OL,3,GNEWSASeaside village taken over by
OL,4,Aoutsiders not speaking Welsh,
OL,5,Acouncillor complains
OL,6,
OL,7,FA seaside village in north Wales has
OL,8,Fbeen "taken over by outsiders" and the
OL,9,FWelsh language is no longer heard in
OL,10,Fits shops and cafes, according to a
OL,11,Flocal councillor.
OL,13,FRobert Llewelyn-Jones made the comments
OL,14,Fduring a planning meeting about a
OL,15,Fretrospective application to retain the
OL,16,Fuse of a holiday let at Llanfaelog,
OL,17,Fnear Rhosneigr, on Anglesey.
OL,19,F"When you visit the shops, people don't
OL,20,Fspeak Welsh," he said.
OL,23,APub: 05-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
